msgid "Sim-to-Real Strategy 5: System Identification With AnchorBench"
msgstr "Sim-to-Real 전략 5: AnchorBench를 활용한 System Identification"

msgid ""
"SO-101 paired trial with SysID actuators on the left and original actuators on the right. Both "
"trials failed: the SysID trial missed the rack, and the original-actuator trial missed the vial "
"grasp."
msgstr ""
"왼쪽 SysID actuator와 오른쪽 original actuator의 SO-101 paired trial입니다. 둘 다 실패했으며 SysID는 rack을, "
"original은 vial grasp를 놓쳤습니다."

msgid "What Do I Need for This Module?"
msgstr "이 Module에 필요한 준비물"

msgid ""
"This module uses videos and published comparisons to explain system identification. You do not "
"need a connected robot or a running workshop container."
msgstr "Video와 공개된 비교로 System Identification을 설명합니다. 연결된 robot이나 실행 중인 workshop container는 필요하지 않습니다."

msgid ""
"The same joint command can produce different motion in simulation and on hardware. **System "
"identification (SysId)** estimates model parameters from measured behavior so that simulation "
"better represents the physical system. Here, you'll compare SO-101 motion with and without an "
"[AnchorBench](https://github.com/NVIDIA/anchor-bench) SysID layer and see how model differences "
"can affect policy behavior."
msgstr ""
"같은 joint command라도 simulation과 hardware의 motion이 다를 수 있습니다. **System Identification (SysId)**은 "
"측정된 동작에서 model parameter를 추정해 simulation이 실제 system을 더 잘 표현하도록 합니다. "
"[AnchorBench](https://github.com/NVIDIA/anchor-bench) SysID layer 유무에 따른 SO-101 motion과 policy "
"동작의 차이를 비교합니다."

msgid "Learning Objectives"
msgstr "학습 목표"

msgid "Explain how measured robot motion informs system identification."
msgstr "측정한 robot motion을 System Identification에 사용하는 방법 설명"

msgid "Recognize differences between baseline, fitted, and measured motion."
msgstr "Baseline, fitted, measured motion의 차이 파악"

msgid "Explain why matched actions and initial conditions matter in an experiment."
msgstr "동일한 action과 초기 조건이 중요한 이유 설명"

msgid "Distinguish actuator-model validation from downstream policy evaluation."
msgstr "Actuator-model 검증과 후속 policy 평가 구분"

msgid "From Measurements to a Simulation Model"
msgstr "측정에서 Simulation Model로"

msgid ""
"A position-controlled joint's response depends on more than its target angle. Drive stiffness and"
" damping, actuator effort limits, armature, and friction affect tracking and settling. A SysId "
"workflow adjusts these parameters to reduce disagreement between simulated motion and physical "
"measurements."
msgstr ""
"Position-controlled joint의 응답은 target angle만으로 결정되지 않습니다. Drive stiffness, damping, effort limit,"
" armature, friction이 tracking과 settling에 영향을 줍니다. SysId는 이런 parameter를 조정해 simulation motion과 실제 "
"측정의 차이를 줄입니다."

msgid ""
"The basic process is to record informative motions, fit a model on a chosen subset, and test it "
"on motions excluded from fitting. A good fit should explain behavior beyond the motions used to "
"tune it. Policy success is a further test: improved motion tracking does not by itself establish "
"better pick-and-place performance."
msgstr ""
"정보가 풍부한 motion을 기록하고 일부로 model을 fitting한 뒤 fitting에 쓰지 않은 motion으로 검증합니다. 좋은 fit은 조정에 쓰지 않은 동작도 "
"설명해야 합니다. Policy 성공은 추가 시험이며 motion tracking 개선만으로 pick-and-place 성능 향상이 입증되지는 않습니다."

msgid "Measure physical motion, fit a simulation model, then validate motion and policy behavior"
msgstr "실제 Motion 측정 → Simulation Model Fitting → Motion과 Policy 동작 검증"

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "Anchor-Lab and AnchorBench"
msgstr "Anchor-Lab and AnchorBench"

msgid ""
"[NVIDIA Anchor-Lab](https://huggingface.co/datasets/nvidia/Anchor-Lab) is a collection of "
"timestamped measurements from physical robot experiments. It covers SO-101 arms and H1/G1 "
"humanoids. The SO-101 recordings include frequency sweeps, backlash-detection motions, and "
"workspace sweeps: different motions reveal different aspects of a robot's response. These "
"measurements provide a reference for calibrating and validating simulation models."
msgstr ""
"[NVIDIA Anchor-Lab](https://huggingface.co/datasets/nvidia/Anchor-Lab)은 SO-101 arm과 H1/G1 "
"humanoid의 실제 실험에서 얻은 timestamp 포함 측정 자료입니다. SO-101에는 frequency sweep, backlash 검출 motion, "
"workspace sweep이 포함됩니다. 각 motion은 응답의 다른 특성을 드러내며 simulation model의 calibration과 검증 기준을 제공합니다."

msgid ""
"The [SO-101 AnchorBench comparison](https://huggingface.co/VigneshBhavan/so101-newton-actuator-"
"ab-paired-checkpoints) shows how fitted actuator parameters can be studied in a policy-learning "
"workflow. Its Hugging Face page brings together baseline and fitted actuator profiles, paired "
"policy checkpoints, reproduction notes, and comparison videos. The accompanying [paired "
"demonstrations](https://huggingface.co/datasets/VigneshBhavan/so101-newton-actuator-ab-paired-"
"demos) use matched commands and scenes to help isolate the effect of the actuator model."
msgstr ""
"[SO-101 AnchorBench 비교](https://huggingface.co/VigneshBhavan/so101-newton-actuator-ab-paired-"
"checkpoints)는 fitted actuator parameter를 policy-learning workflow에서 연구하는 예시입니다. Baseline/fitted "
"profile, paired policy checkpoint, 재현 안내, 비교 video를 제공합니다. [Paired "
"demonstration](https://huggingface.co/datasets/VigneshBhavan/so101-newton-actuator-ab-paired-"
"demos)은 command와 scene을 맞춰 actuator model 효과를 분리합니다."

msgid ""
"The published bundle supplies a fitted profile and reproduction records, but not a complete "
"command sequence for fitting a new AnchorBench model from Anchor-Lab telemetry."
msgstr ""
"공개 bundle은 fitted profile과 재현 기록을 제공하지만 Anchor-Lab telemetry로 새 AnchorBench model을 fitting하는 전체 "
"명령 순서는 포함하지 않습니다."

msgid "Teleop Comparison: Default and SysID Assets"
msgstr "Teleoperation 비교: Default와 SysID Asset"

msgid ""
"A poorly tuned robot asset can move differently from the physical robot it represents. This "
"teleoperation comparison overlays the default SO-101 asset, the asset with a fitted SysID layer, "
"and the measured hardware motion. The separation between them illustrates the actuation gap."
msgstr ""
"제대로 조정되지 않은 robot asset은 실제 robot과 다르게 움직일 수 있습니다. Default SO-101, fitted SysID layer 적용 asset, "
"실제 측정 motion을 겹쳐 차이로 actuation gap을 보여줍니다."

msgid "Color"
msgstr "색상"

msgid "What it shows"
msgstr "의미"

