msgstr "Default USD asset 위에 SysID USD layer 적용"

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "**Light blue**"
msgstr "**Light blue**"

msgid ""
"Joint values read back from the physical SO-101 being driven. This readback adds a little more "
"delay."
msgstr "실제로 제어 중인 SO-101에서 읽은 joint value. Readback에 약간의 추가 지연이 있습니다."

msgid ""
"Compare how closely the simulated motion follows the light-blue hardware readback. Account for "
"the readback delay when interpreting timing differences; not every visible lag comes from the "
"actuator model."
msgstr ""
"Simulation motion이 light-blue hardware readback을 얼마나 잘 따르는지 비교하세요. Timing을 해석할 때 readback delay도 "
"고려해야 하며, 모든 지연이 actuator model 때문은 아닙니다."

msgid "Example SysID Motion: Chirp Sweep"
msgstr "SysID Motion 예시: Chirp Sweep"

msgid ""
"A chirp sweep gradually changes the frequency of an oscillating command. Watch the lag, "
"amplitude, and settling of the measured motion as the sweep progresses. A single static pose "
"would not reveal these response differences."
msgstr ""
"Chirp sweep은 진동 명령의 frequency를 점차 바꿉니다. 진행에 따른 measured motion의 lag, amplitude, settling을 보세요. "
"하나의 정적 pose로는 이런 응답 차이를 볼 수 없습니다."

msgid ""
"Six joint-response plots for the chirp sweep, comparing dashed commanded trajectories with solid "
"motor encoder measurements as frequency increases. Arm positions are in degrees; gripper opening "
"is in percent."
msgstr ""
"Frequency 증가에 따른 commanded trajectory(점선)와 motor encoder 측정(실선)의 6개 joint-response plot입니다. Arm "
"position 단위는 degree, gripper opening은 percent입니다."

msgid ""
"Joint responses from the chirp sweep above. Dashed lines show the commanded motion; solid lines "
"show motor encoder measurements. Notice where the measured motion lags or has a smaller amplitude"
" as the oscillations get faster."
msgstr "위 chirp sweep의 joint 응답입니다. 진동이 빨라질 때 측정 motion이 늦거나 amplitude가 작아지는 구간을 보세요."

msgid "Workshop Comparison: SysId and Original Actuators"
msgstr "Workshop 비교: SysId와 Original Actuator"

msgid ""
"Watch these 10 paired trials with SysId actuators on the left and original actuators on the "
"right. The video plays at 5× speed."
msgstr "왼쪽 SysId와 오른쪽 original actuator의 paired trial 10개입니다. 5배속으로 재생됩니다."

msgid ""
"The policy used here was not trained to robust task performance, but the comparison makes "
"failures while moving toward the vial visible. Focus on the approach: does the gripper reach the "
"vial in a position where it can grasp it? Use these observations to distinguish approach failures"
" from problems during grasping or placement."
msgstr ""
"이 policy는 task를 견고하게 수행할 정도로 학습되지 않았지만 vial로 접근할 때의 실패를 보여줍니다. Gripper가 grasp 가능한 위치에 도달하는지 집중해서 "
"보세요. Approach 실패와 grasp 또는 placement 문제를 구분합니다."

msgid "Simulation Evaluation Results"
msgstr "Simulation 평가 결과"

msgid ""
"In a separate simulation comparison, we evaluated two policies with both actuator profiles. Each "
"cell below reports successful placements out of **100 trials**, using the same scene resets, a "
"16-action execution horizon, and a 30-second trial limit."
msgstr ""
"별도의 simulation 비교에서 두 policy를 두 actuator profile로 각각 평가했습니다. 각 셀은 같은 scene reset, 16-action "
"execution horizon, 30초 trial limit으로 실행한 **100 trial** 중 placement 성공 수입니다."

